{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Write for yourselves.</b> A commandment that Moses write it, and also everyone who understands shall write it." "<b>and teach it.</b> The difficult accents, that he expound to them." "<b>Put it in their mouths.</b> That they know it by recitation." "And the word ולמדה is also like שימה in being foreign, for the rule is for the heh of ולמדה to have kamatz, and under the dalet a small patach." "<b>for an eternal witness in the children of Israel.</b> Joined to the reason with כי אביאנו. Also possible for it to be disjunctive on account of וענתה, like the meaning of לא תענה ברעך, as if the song testifies in response to those who say: Why has all this found us?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:43.539712284Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}